## Decisions log

- **(v0.10.11) Bounce or roll, decided by how hard it lands.** The 1.5 m/s threshold, the
  3 m/s² friction and the 6 m/s cap were all already in this document; the code applied the
  bounce every resting tick and so never reached the roll. Fixed toward the document rather
  than the document toward the code: "his head can crash along the slope" needs a roll.
- **(v0.10.11) The roll cap is on speed across, and holds on a slope.** Capping before
  gravity's pull was added let a head run a slope at 6.5 m/s; the cap is now applied to what
  the roll keeps.
- **(v0.10.11) A rolling head does not bounce at a change of slope.** At the foot of a slope
  it used to bounce four times and reach level ground with half its speed.
- **(v0.10.11) Whether a boss's head should roll faster, last longer or be thrown harder is
  boss design** (`FOES.gdd` §8.2) and is not decided; today both heads are the same head.

